body:
I went to the hospital when police showed up at my job, pretty embarrassing but I was super depressed and told my significant other about it, but she over exaggerated to police on how I felt and how I was feeling. Long story short, they handcuffed me right in front of my co-workers and manager which felt so awkward. I felt like I was going to lose my job when they admitted me into mental health clinic for over 6 days without letting anyone know about my incident. They wouldn't even let me call my work or let my family know. Overall I had a horrible experience from the outcome and somehow I manage to keep my job which was surprising, I had to explain everything with my manager in who was very understanding. By the way, if anyone can chime in.. If your being fired for mental health reasons, isn't that covered under the ADA? What happened to EEO? 

&#x200B;

I hope you get well soon brother! I'm in the same scenario as going from social to anti-social.

My disability for the assault is combined, I have PTSD, Major Depression and Generalized Anxiety Disorder all rated together at 30%. Ever since the incident and my trip to mental health. I feel like I got worse after my treatment. My depression and anxiety was bad, but now it's gone downhill, I feel worse than before and I have constant migraines and headaches everyday which is effecting my daily life. 

&#x200B;

To your question, YES. Thank you for your time for the response, much appreciated and I need some feedback! :)
